okf_version: "1.0"
task: "Support the Codex desktop app (Windows Store OpenAI.Codex) as a Ciel Runtime execution runtime, with an isolated CODEX_HOME and channel (SSE) injection."
reported: "User, 2026-09-23: 'codex app desktop 버전도 실행 런타임으로 지원'; choices: separate CODEX_HOME, include channel SSE injection."
design:
  attach: "Ciel starts `codex app-server --listen ws://127.0.0.1:<router+20>` through the existing run_codex_app_server (same -c routing args), waits for /readyz, then starts ChatGPT.exe with CODEX_APP_SERVER_WS_URL, CODEX_HOME=<config>/codex-desktop/<workspace>/codex-home, CODEX_ELECTRON_USER_DATA_PATH + --user-data-dir=<.../electron-user-data>. Routing therefore never depends on config.toml; config.toml is only seeded once from ~/.codex, auth.json follows the source when newer."
  injection: "codex_desktop_injection.CodexDesktopChannelInjector: second JSON-RPC client over a stdlib WebSocket adapter (codex_app_server_websocket.CodexAppServerWebSocketProcess, no Origin header) reusing CodexAppServerClient unchanged. Reads runtime inputs after the shared channel cursor; router-transport messages are left for the router; hidden/superseded ones pass the cursor; others go in via turn/start (idle) or turn/steer (running turn). Status submitted on send, replied/failed from turn/completed."
  hook: "run_codex_app_server(..., desktop=callable) replaces only the final process step; launch mode label codex-desktop-router; last_launch_runtime maps it to codex-desktop."
files:
  new: "ciel_runtime_support/codex_desktop_runtime.py, codex_desktop_injection.py, codex_app_server_websocket.py; tests/test_codex_desktop_runtime.py and tests/test_codex_desktop_injection.py (24 tests together, including WebSocket framing/handshake cases); docs/Codex-Desktop.md."
  changed: "runtime_launch.run_codex_app_server (desktop hook), cli_dispatch (positional codex-desktop/codex-desktop-app/launch-codex-desktop, --ca-runtime value, last set, dispatch), cli_application_context routes, launch_state, prelaunch (menu action with the Codex provider gate), prelaunch_launch_panel/preference/shell_context, prelaunch_panel_projection, cli_usage, ciel_runtime.py wiring (net 0 lines: four codex_config imports merged to stay at the 4980-line budget), README, CLI-Reference, CHANGELOG."
e2e:
  setup: "Isolated config copy (scratchpad e2e-cfg, provider deepseek), temp workspace, router port 19941, every inherited CIEL_RUNTIME_* variable unset first (see hazard)."
  result: "`ciel_runtime.py cli --ca-runtime codex-desktop`: app-server ready on ws://127.0.0.1:19961, app log 'Starting app-server connection hostId=local transport=websocket' / 'Codex CLI initialized'. POST /ca/chat/notify id=1 -> codex_desktop_channel_injected via=turn/start (1 s) -> router POST /v1/responses 200 -> deepseek -> agent message 'desktop-injection-ok' -> status queued/submitted/replied. id=2 started a turn; id=3 sent 12 s later went in via=turn/steer into that same turn (rollout shows it inside turn 01a0cf0b...). Rollout session_meta model_provider=ciel-runtime, cli_version 0.156.0. Killing the app window process: codex_desktop_session_ended, ports 19961 and 19941 closed, 0 leftover processes, the user's own app instance (pid 83404) untouched."
  not_shown_in_ui: "The new isolated profile opened on the app's first-run onboarding ('Which best describes your work?'); I did not fill that form, so the chat view itself was not captured. Turn 2 then waited on the app's approval prompt for an escalated command (Start-Sleep with sandbox_permissions require_escalated), which is the app's own approval gate."
  model_side_note: "deepseek first emitted a tool call named functions__exec_command, which app-server rejected ('unsupported call'); the model then used the code-mode exec tool correctly. Not investigated further."
  exit_code: "The launcher exited 127 after I force-killed the app process; a normal window close was not exercised, so the exit code for that path is not verified."
hazard:
  inherited_env: "A shell started from a Ciel session carries CIEL_RUNTIME_PROVIDER, CIEL_RUNTIME_LAUNCH_CWD, CIEL_RUNTIME_STATE_DIR and CIEL_RUNTIME_WORKSPACE_STATE_DIR of that live session. The first two E2E attempts inherited them: the provider override switched the copied config to anthropic (launch blocked), and the launch identified itself as the c:\\users\\djlov\\ciel-runtime workspace - past the provider gate it would have run the router-client cleanup for the live session. Both attempts stopped at the provider gate; the user's config.json was verified unchanged (provider nvidia-hosted, mtime before the runs)."
tests: "scripts/run_test_group.py with every CIEL_RUNTIME_* unset: unit 1608 OK (skipped=45), router 1153 OK, channel 423 OK (skipped=80), runtime 320 OK (skipped=19) - runtime is the previous 296 plus the 24 new cases. ruff clean on ciel_runtime.py, ciel_runtime_support and the new tests."
not_done:
  - "Not committed, pushed or deployed."
  - "UI screenshot of an injected turn in the chat view (blocked on the onboarding form)."
  - "The launch-menu entry is covered by code and the passing groups only; it was not driven interactively."
  - "A normal window close (rather than a forced kill) was not exercised."
